{
 "what": "Plug-tip pose relative to port 2 at the end of the approach (pre-insert), per episode, in sim with full DR. This is the start distribution Part 4 (insertion RL) must absorb.",
 "frame_and_units": "port-2 frame: x across the panel (m->mm), y up, z out of the panel (gap); rx, ry = rotation of the reader about port x / y (deg; tilt = |(rx, ry)|), roll about the port axis (deg). Signed mean/std and percentiles of |error|. gap_error = gap - stop distance.",
 "how_measured": "scripts/task/eval_approach.py (2 seeds x 512 worlds per configuration, GPU runtime): ZED RGB estimate of the PC pose (learned CNN on DR renders) -> left press hold (guarded) -> right arm IK move to 30 mm in front of the estimated port with the nominal in-hand pose (true joints carry the encoder-offset error, true reader the randomized in-hand pose) -> visual servo on the right wrist RGB (learned plug-to-port estimator, coarse net, fine net below 12 mm) with smooth moves and Coulomb feed-forward -> privileged measurement of the live plug-tip pose in the live port frame. DR: PC layout +/-3 cm/+/-10 deg, PC feet mu U(0.3, 0.9), arm Coulomb x U(0.5, 1.3), gravity jitter, encoder offsets +/-1.5 deg (joints 2-5), latency 0-1 step, in-hand +/-3 mm / +/-8 deg (confirmed 60-deg grasp, provisional numbers), policy/v1 visual DR (appearance, lighting, image noise, camera pose up to 2x real: ZED 8.6 mm / 1.2 deg, right wrist 10.2 mm / 2.4 deg, intrinsics).",
